        "revision": "c451f4d674096e6e6f1cc5d0abb6794bda638304",
        "filename": "MiniCPM5-2B-F16.gguf",
        "rationale": "Top-trending text-generation release of the day (upstream openbmb/MiniCPM5-2B, trend 929). A 2.5B dense LlamaForCausalLM with GQA and a 131k context is a materially different efficiency tradeoff from every installed model (smallest installed is gpt-oss:20b; baseline is a 30B-A3B MoE at Q4_K_M). F16 is the publisher's reference file, so the battery measures the model rather than a quantization choice. Publisher-official GGUF, Apache-2.0, single root-level file, 5.04 GB. Comparison question: can a 2B dense model pass the exact-output checks, and what is its throughput against the coder baseline.",
